      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THUNDERING SOUL (1) is hard to look past after scoring well first-up here and justifying his firm market support. His home record over this trip gives him a strong base to repeat. PROVANCE (4) is the danger off stronger recent assignments, with his sixth in a CG BM78 at Doomben easier to accept now he returns from Saturday company and has a previous win at this track. His Ipswich fourth two back was also sound after being forced wide. JEMELDI (3) was behind THUNDERING SOUL last start but still worked home into third after beginning slowly, and now meets him with a 2kg swing which could prove decisive. MR EVANS (7) also comes through the picnics but arrives in winning form and is a distance specialist.",
